(a) No retail dealer for distilled spirits shall keep in stock, display, sell, or offer to sell, at any place of business licensed hereunder, any other product or commodity except the following:
(1) Wines, when properly licensed;
(2) Malt beverages, when properly licensed;
(3) Beverages containing no alcohol commonly used to dilute distilled spirits, and not to be opened on the premises;
(4) Tobacco products;
(5) Ice to be sold in sealed containers only and not to be opened on the premises; and
(6) Paper, Styrofoam or plastic cups.
Beverages containing no alcohol and commonly used to dilute distilled spirits may be dispensed through the use of vending machines, but no alcoholic beverages shall be dispensed through such vending machines.
(b) Licenses shall be issued only for off premises consumption except for licensees holding valid licenses for on premises consumption of malt beverages.
( Ord. of 7-21-2009 , § 10)

